      "id": "187",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 187,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Verb + にいく combines the verb stem with にいく to express going somewhere to do something (e.g., 食べに行く = 'go to eat'). In contrast, ていく (Verb + て + いく) expresses sequential actions (e.g., 食べて行く = 'eat, then go') or actions that progress over time (e.g., 上手くなっていく = 'get better over time').",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 48,
          "slug": "verb-にいく",
          "title": "Verb + にいく",
          "meaning": "To go ~, To go in order to ~",
          "level": "JLPT5",
          "type_pascal": "GrammarPoint",
          "type_snake": "grammar_point"
        },
