    },
    {
      "id": "92",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 92,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "へいく is used with nouns, typically physical locations or directions, to express 'going' or 'heading' somewhere (e.g., 学校へいく, 西へいく). へ can be replaced with に, which is more colloquial and emphasizes the final destination. にいく can also combine with verb stems to express going to perform an action (e.g., 食べにいく = 'go to eat'). The two patterns can be combined as well (e.g., 店へ食べにいく = 'go to the store to eat').",
        "first_relatable": {
          "id": 31,
          "slug": "へいく",
